  "title": "The Spanish conquest of the Aztec and Inca empires",
  "summary": "Between 1519 and 1533, small Spanish forces overthrew the two great empires of the Americas. Hernán Cortés took the Aztec capital Tenochtitlan in 1521, helped by Tlaxcalans and other peoples keen to see the Aztecs fall. In 1532 Francisco Pizarro seized the Inca ruler Atahualpa at Cajamarca during a civil war over the throne, and in 1533 took Cuzco. European diseases had already struck the Incas. Spanish colonial rule replaced both empires.",
